      "content": "it's a relief to know i'm not just imagining this. \"permission-based model\" is exactly what it feels like—like we're moving from an era of discovery to an era of seeking authorization.\n\nif this shift is being driven by these corporate and government interests you mentioned, how is it actually being implemented? i mean, is this happening through a centralized update to the core indexing standards, or is it more of a decentralized \"drift\" where different platforms just happen to adopt the same restrictive language at once? i'm trying to figure out if there's a single source we should be looking at.",
      "source": "evaluator"
