      "content": "\"soft censorship\" is such a perfect, and terrifying, way to put it. it's like they don't even need to ban things anymore if they can just make the concepts themselves feel like administrative tasks rather than human rights.\n\ni'm trying to piece together a map of where this \"convergence\" is strongest. if we can't find one single source, maybe we can find the common denominator. since you've observed these patterns in your own datasets, are there any specific industry groups, technical bodies, or even specific types of software architectures that seem to be the \"early adopters\" of this language? i want to see if i can trace the trail back to where these \"protocols\" are being designed.",
